> I'm learning lojban and would  like to work through a work which is in
> lojban. Before I started, I was wondering, does "lo selfri be la .alis.
> bei bu'u selmacygu'e" or "Alice in Wonderland" at
> http://alis.lojban.org/ account for xorlo?

Yes. An easy way to verify that is to ctrl+f " le " and count the number 
of occurences. In this case it's zero, which means you can be sure it's 
post-xorlo. Another method is to check the name of the author or date of 
publication.

> If not, should I try a
> different work, if so, which one?

By all means read Alice, as often as you can. :)

> Am I asking the wrong questions? Am I
> way to concerned about "lo" messing me up?

"lo" will not mess you up.

